{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/117030","id":3349879560,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc7HqxsI","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117030","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117030.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117030.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117030","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/117030/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/117030/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117030/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/93d29e7d96b9415bcda6deabb78b2b546883f5f0","number":117030,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Use IDs instead of hashes for TrackCache keys","user":{"login":"ugursoy","id":15056545,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MDU2NTQ1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15056545?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ugursoy","html_url":"https://github.com/ugursoy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ugursoy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ugursoy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ugursoy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ugursoy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ugursoy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ugursoy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ugursoy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ugursoy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ugursoy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Fixes: https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/116231\r\n\r\nHello, \r\n\r\nI've been tracking this issue since `4.6.0-stable` made it apparent. This is a solution that implements re-hashing on hash collisions for `track_cache`. As far as I'm aware, using `StringName` for hash was the latest solution proposed here (https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110439) by @beicause for hash collisions. I pulled the last commit there and tested it, and found it decreasing the performance a bit. `uint32_t` comparisons are faster so I wanted to keep them.\r\n\r\nIn order to both fix the collision issue and keep using `uint32_t`, I made 3 implementations and tested them:\r\n1. Dynamic double hash (Using double `AHashMap`)\r\n\t- `track_cache` holds `(TypeHash, HashBucket *)` pairs where `HashBucket` contains a `union` that is either a `TrackCache *` or another `AHashMap`\r\n2. Adding a linked list in `TrackCache` struct\r\n\t- the `struct` simply holds `next` and `prev` pointers\r\n\t- adds to the list in case of collisions and iterates the whole list per lookup\r\n3. Re-hashing the hash that collides with a `uint32_t probe` value until it no longer collides within the `track_cache`\r\n\t- Nothing changes, just the `thash` value is probed when a collision is detected\r\n\t- All hashes are inserted into a static `AHashMap` and that map is checked during insertion\r\n\r\nThese solutions are either proposed or mentioned in other hash related PR discussions: ([the one referenced above](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110439) and https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110400)(https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110439).\r\n\r\nI tried not to touch other parts of the code and only focus on hash. My benchmark results for the provided MRP in (https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110474) with my system (Ryzen5 1600, RTX2060) is as follows:\r\n\r\n  | Stable | Dynamic Double Hash | Rehash | Linked List | StringName\r\n-- | -- | -- | -- | -- | --\r\nAvg FPS | 127.72 | 116.38 | 127.5 | 124.84 | 110.04\r\nAvg MSPF | 7.83 | 8.59 | 7.84 | 8.01 | 9.08\r\n\r\nSince that mrp does not contain any hash collisions, these can be considered as amortized performance. \r\n\r\nAll except rehashing, requires additional checks to see if the hash key maps to a unique track or a bucket; and another lookup after that in case of collisions. So as expected, their runtime performances are worse (more than I expected). Also, collisions occur very rarely, so making additional checks that costs a few frames for a very rare case made no sense to me. Therefore, moving the cost to track creation time seemed like the best option. \r\n\r\nMy implementation is not exactly what @TokageItLab proposed (with deferred calls and all) because I didn't understand how to do that :laughing:.\r\n\r\nI tested this PR with [mrp-rehash.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/25722014/mrp-rehash.zip) . It contains 3 tracks in animation player that generates the same hash in v4.6. Adding/removing, undo/redo, works fine in my tests. I tested these only in 2D.\r\n\r\n\r\n","labels":[{"id":73330064,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2NA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/bug","name":"bug","description":"","color":"ff6055","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":2666705648,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNjY2NzA1NjQ4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:animation","name":"topic:animation","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":14236899,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4A2Tzj","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/24","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/24","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/24/labels","number":24,"state":"closed","title":"4.7","description":"","creator":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/u